# Rocdown CLI

This is the `rocdown` binary (`rocci-rocdown-cli`). It is not the Rocci CLI.
Rocci commands live in the [Rocci CLI reference](/docs/reference/cli/).

Source-checkout spelling:

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- COMMAND
```

| Command | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `check [ROOT]` | Catalog, links, includes, assets. No Roc compile |
| `test [ROOT]` | Run `:example` commands that declare `test` |
| `build [ROOT]` | Write the static (and hybrid) tree |
| `view [ROOT]` | Watch, rebuild, serve, optional preview window. Hybrid sites proxy islands. `run` is a deprecated alias |
| `package [ROOT]` | CDN archive plus optional island binary |
| `serve [DIST]` | Serve an existing `dist/` on loopback |
| `serve-islands [ROOT]` | Island HTTP service only |
| `inspect ast FILE` | Rocdown AST |
| `inspect artifacts [ROOT]` | Planned output and page kinds |

`rocdown` refuses OKF knowledge records; use `rocci-okf`.

See [Write Rocdown pages](/rocdown/pages/), [Article blocks](/rocdown/article-blocks/),
and [Site configuration](/rocdown/site-config/).
